{"id":1087,"profile":{"ID":2585,"title":"Chris Madsen","content":"","attr_title":"","menu_type":"profile","url":"\/profile\/chris-madsen\/","slug":"chris-madsen","parent":"2584","coords":"","offset":"","confirmation_status":"","event_length_seconds":"","point_of_contact":"","guest_type":"","event_type":"","appearance_type":"","notes":"","classes":[""],"post":{"ID":1087,"post_author":"1","post_date":"2021-09-29 02:09:44","post_date_gmt":"2021-09-29 02:09:44","post_content":"Chris worked 20 years in behavioral health administration and programming before experiencing social presence via VR in 2013. VR changed his professional trajectory when he recognized the disruptive implications remote, immersive, shared experiences, unbound from the physical restraints and proximity requirements of the real world, will have on the way humans work, learn, and socialize.\n\nListed by Onalytica as a Top 100 influencer in both AR and VR, Chris is particularly noted for keeping a close pulse on the social, educational, artistic and entertainment spaces of the XR movement.\n\nChris has held a variety of roles including Social VR Liaison for the leading Virtual Reality tech blog \u2018Road to VR\u2019, co-founder of Utah VR and Silicon Slopes (AR\/VR chapter), Edge of Discovery Ambassador, Siggraph judge, XR consultant\/speaker, and Director of AR\/VR at Morph 3D where he co-developed portable and persistent avatar systems.\n\nChris is currently serving as Senior Sales Engineer for ENGAGE XR, delivering virtual collaboration, communication, training, education, events and creative solutions to a growing global market transitioning to the metaverse","post_title":"Chris Madsen","post_excerpt":"","post_status":"publish","comment_status":"closed","ping_status":"closed","post_password":"","post_name":"chris-madsen","to_ping":"","pinged":"","post_modified":"2022-11-30 15:18:35","post_modified_gmt":"2022-11-30 15:18:35","post_content_filtered":"","post_parent":0,"guid":"https:\/\/webxr.events\